# The counter at the shell's priority (roadmap l4.md L2): it never waits, so
# only the time slices let the shell in; the shell still answers. The shell
# is the shell in C, a process among init's (os-server.md P12).
program: shell
define: TEST_COUNTER_SAME
define: TEST_THREAD_REPORT
keys: echo one\necho two\n
---
rx286, test build
/mnt/rx286$ echo one
one
/mnt/rx286$ echo two
two
/mnt/rx286$
rx286: thread root ran
rx286: thread printer ran
